>
>Yup.  Nethack is running in my user directory on our system as SUID.  All I
>have needed to do is make the executable and its directory world-readable.
>I have often heard that it is somewhat a better idea to make the game SGID
>"games" instead, if you can (chmod g+s nethack).  I think the S*ID stuff is
>pretty secure if handled properly, but be forewarned that it still might
>pose a security hazard.

Basically, there are a few rules to follow.  Never make a shell
script suid.  This poses numerous risks, which I won't go into! ;)
Also, avoid suid unless absolutely necessary, which in this case
it is NOT.  If any executable must be made 'sticky', sgid is the
way to go.  Also, you can make a special group 'nethack', make the
group of the directory be nethack, and sgid the executable to
nethack.  This prevents nethack from modifying any other games
without affecting its playability.

